WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
You need to protect your purchasing power of your savings against the effects of inflation.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.800
You see, as prices rise, each dollar is able to buy less.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.400
Makes sense right?

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.100
If the dollars you have saved for the future don't increase in value by at least as much

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:25.100
as inflation, the purchasing power of those savings will fall, which pretty much defeats

6
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.800
the purpose of saving.

7
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.400
Remember inflation?

8
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.000
Inflation is the increase in the average level of prices in the economy.
